course: dictionary
lesson: 6287
title: One word, three jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Moo is a small word that can do three different jobs. As a noun, it is the sound itself: «the cows mooed» tells you the cows made their long, low sound. As a verb, it is the action of making that sound. As an interjection, it is said on its own, like a quick «moo!»
explain: Context tells you which job the word is doing. In «Old MacDonald Had a Farm», «with a moo-moo here» is the cow's sound. In the Wonderland story, the sobs turn into «the lowing (mooing) of cattle», so mooing names a sound that cattle make. Read the words around moo and ask which job it is doing.
explain: Some meanings are not about animals at all. In UK talk, «silly moo» is an informal, rude name for a silly person. Ask yourself: is this sentence about a farm, or about a person? The clues around the word show you which meaning fits.
fact: Moo is a noun (a moo, moos) and a verb (to moo).
fact: The verb forms are moo, moos, mooed and mooing.
fact: «The cows mooed» means the cows made a long, low sound.
fact: «Silly moo» is informal UK slang for a silly person, and it can be rude, so do not use it at school.
fact: In French, a cow says «meuh», which is the French word for moo.
exercise: «The cows mooed in the field all morning.» What does mooed mean here? | They jumped over the gate | They ran away from the farm | They went to sleep | *They made their long, low sound
exercise: The French animal noises include «meuh». Which English sound is that? | *moo | quack | woof | miaow
exercise: Ella hears someone say, «Don't be such a silly moo!» What does silly moo mean? | *A silly person, said in a rude, informal way | A cow with a silly name | A noise a farm animal makes | A kind friend
test: In «She heard a long moo from the barn», what job does moo do? | Verb, an action | Interjection, said on its own | *Noun, the sound itself | Adjective, describing the barn
test: Pick the past tense of moo to finish: «The cow ___ all night.» | mooing | moos | moo | *mooed
exam: In «the lowing (mooing) of cattle», what does mooing describe? | Bells ringing on sheep | *The long, low sound of cows | A type of game | Crying loudly
